import json,re,sys
from pathlib import Path
root=Path(sys.argv[1]);data={}
CASES={
 'multibyte':('The message line that never ended',
  'The screen row holds eighty characters, one of them two bytes wide, so the text needs eighty-one bytes plus its terminator - one byte past the wide-count limit the conversion used. The original truncates exactly at the limit and writes no terminator, and the caller measures the buffer as a string: with the buffer junked and no zero anywhere, the measurement runs through all thousand twenty-four stale bytes. The correction bounds the conversion by the size of the caller buffer, so the full text converts and terminates at eighty-one.'),
 'wide':('A wide terminal: 301 columns of four-byte text',
  'The message line is read the way the Borg reads it: the full terminal width (three hundred characters here, each four bytes in UTF-8) into a 1024-byte buffer followed by a guard area. The original limit of one byte per character stops after seventy-five characters without a terminator: unterminated, but nothing written past the buffer. The earlier fix shape, a limit of MB_CUR_MAX bytes per character, is not tied to the buffer: it writes 1201 bytes, 177 of them past the buffer (AddressSanitizer: stack-buffer-overflow). The buffer-size bound converts the 255 characters that fit, terminates at 1020 and writes nothing past the buffer.'),
 'control':('Control: a pure-ASCII row',
  'The same row with every character one byte wide fits the old limit too: both variants terminate identically at eighty, and the complete log is byte-identical.')}
for mode,(label,explanation) in CASES.items():
 item={'label':label,'explanation':explanation}
 for phase in ('before','interim','after'):
  raw=(root/f'{phase}-{mode}.log').read_text()
  entry={'raw':raw,'passed':'native-c/text-287 finished: 1/1 passed' in raw}
  for tag in ('RATING ','OUTCOME '):
   match=re.search(re.escape(tag)+r'(.*)',raw)
   entry[tag.split()[0].lower()]=match[1].strip() if match else None
  araw=(root/f'{phase}-asan-{mode}.log').read_text()
  report=re.search(r'ERROR: AddressSanitizer: (\S+)',araw)
  entry['asan']=report[1] if report else 'no report'
  item[phase]=entry
 data[mode]=item
html='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>The message line that never ended</title><style>body{margin:0;background:#f4f1ea;color:#253a3c;font:18px/1.6 system-ui}main{max-width:1100px;margin:auto;padding:32px 24px}h1{font-size:40px;line-height:1.2}h2{font-size:24px}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr 1fr;gap:20px}.card{background:white;border:1px solid #cbd6d0;border-radius:12px;padding:24px;margin:18px 0}.cards .card{border-top:6px solid #648e80}.num{font-size:34px;font-weight:750}select,button{font:inherit;max-width:100%;padding:10px;border:1px solid #aabdb5;border-radius:7px;background:white}button{cursor:pointer;margin:14px 8px 0 0}button.active{background:#24685d;color:white}.summary{background:#e6eee6;padding:20px;border-left:5px solid #377367}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;font:13px/1.5 monospace;max-height:330px;overflow:auto}details{background:white;padding:20px;margin:20px 0}summary{font-weight:700;cursor:pointer}@media(max-width:650px){.cards{grid-template-columns:1fr}h1{font-size:30px}}</style><main><p>Recorded native screen-text conversions</p><h1>The message line that never ended</h1><p>The Borg reads the message line from the screen as wide characters and converts it back to bytes - with a limit of one byte per wide character. A multibyte character occupies more than one byte, so a line whose byte length lands exactly on the limit was truncated without its terminating zero, and the uninitialized caller buffer was then trimmed and measured as a string: stale stack bytes parsed as message text, producing phantom monsters in the supplied replay evidence. The correction passes the size of the caller buffer, converts at most one byte less and always terminates. A third panel shows the earlier fix shape (a limit of MB_CUR_MAX bytes per character), which terminated the short line but could write past the buffer on a wide terminal.</p><section class="card"><label for="scenario">Choose a recorded situation</label><br><select id="scenario"></select><p id="explanation"></p><br><button data-step="0">Terminated</button></section><div class="cards"><section id="original" class="card"><h2>Original</h2><div class="num"></div><p class="state"></p><p class="asan"></p></section><section id="interim" class="card"><h2>Earlier fix shape</h2><div class="num"></div><p class="state"></p><p class="asan"></p></section><section id="compared" class="card"><h2>Corrected</h2><div class="num"></div><p class="state"></p><p class="asan"></p></section></div><p class="summary" id="outcome"></p><h2>What the control establishes</h2><p>A pure-ASCII row fits the old limit as well: both variants terminate identically with byte-identical logs - the correction changes only the multibyte boundary case.</p><details><summary>Experiment conditions and limits</summary><p>Native Human Warrior, seed one thousand, a UTF-8 locale (the multibyte conversion only widens in a multibyte locale), a hand-painted screen row of eighty characters with exactly one two-byte character, and a caller buffer deliberately junked with no zero anywhere so an unterminated conversion is visible as a full-buffer measurement. This isolates the conversion bound, not the full message-parsing chain; the phantom-monster consequence is the supplied harness evidence, not claimed here. No death or survival claim. The wide case reads a 301-column row into a 1024-byte buffer the way borg_get_messages() does; in the normal build a guard area after the buffer counts any write past it, and the AddressSanitizer build uses a standalone buffer so such a write is reported.</p></details><details><summary>Recorded native output</summary><h3>Original</h3><pre id="original-log"></pre><h3>Earlier fix shape</h3><pre id="interim-log"></pre><h3>Corrected</h3><pre id="compared-log"></pre></details><p>Canonical report: <a href="https://github.com/diegoami/neo-angband-tracker/issues/287">issue287</a>.</p></main><script>
const data=__DATA__;const select=document.getElementById('scenario');for(const [key,c] of Object.entries(data)){let o=document.createElement('option');o.value=key;o.textContent=c.label;select.append(o)}function draw(){let c=data[select.value];document.getElementById('explanation').textContent=c.explanation;for(const [panel,phase] of [['original','before'],['interim','interim'],['compared','after']]){let d=c[phase],p=document.getElementById(panel);let r=d.rating||'';let m=r.match(/terminated=(\\d+) strnlen=(\\d+)(?: guard_overwritten=(\\d+))?/);p.querySelector('.num').textContent=m?('Terminated: '+(m[1]==='1'?'yes':'no')+', length '+m[2]+(m[3]!==undefined?', bytes past buffer '+m[3]:'')):'n/a';p.querySelector('.asan').textContent='AddressSanitizer: '+d.asan;p.querySelector('.state').textContent=d.outcome||'';document.getElementById(panel+'-log').textContent=d.raw}document.getElementById('outcome').textContent={multibyte:'The original leaves the conversion unterminated - the measurement runs through all 1024 stale bytes; the correction terminates at 81, the full text.',control:'The ASCII row was never at risk: terminated at 80 either way, byte for byte.',wide:'The original is unterminated but stays inside the buffer; the earlier fix shape writes 177 bytes past it; the correction terminates at 1020 and stays inside.'}[select.value];}select.addEventListener('change',draw);draw();</script></html>'''
(root/'replay.html').write_text(html.replace('__DATA__',json.dumps(data).replace('<','\\u003c')))
(root/'replay-data.json').write_text(json.dumps(data,indent=2)+'\n')
print('Open in your browser:',root/'replay.html')
